Done. Lesson written to `courses/optyka-vs-sar-porownawcza-wizja-komputerowa/lessons/gauss-median-bilateral-na-optyce.json` and `LessonSchema.safeParse` returns `success: true`.
**Layout** (2 theory beats + 5 widgets, within the 1 theory + 2–5 widget budget):
1. **theory** `po-co-filtrowac` (266 words) — sets up the optical-noise baseline ($I = I_{\text{clean}} + n$) before SAR breaks it next lesson; inline image `cameraman-clean-vs-noisy.png`.
2. **demo** `demo-gauss` — canonical `gauss` demo on `/demo-images/cameraman.jpg`, σ ∈ [0, 6], default 1.5.
3. **theory** `trzy-filtry` (273 words) — Gauss/median/bilateral side-by-side table + bilateral KaTeX formula; inline image `gauss-median-bilateral-triple.png`.
4. **plotImage** `plot-step-edge` — 1D step-edge comparison plot with mandatory axes/labels/legend; PNG hash verified to be reproducible from the embedded `sourceCode`.
5. **quiz** `check-kiedy-ktory` — single-answer, distractors picked to diagnose the common "one filter does it all" misconception.
6. **code** `exercise-trzy-filtry` — `denoise(img)` returning `{gauss, median, bilateral}` via scipy/skimage; 4 tests (shape, spike removal, smoothness, edge preservation); `inputs` + `outputMedia` referencing locally-cached PNGs; `requiresPackages: ["scikit-image", "Pillow"]`.
7. **sandbox** `sandbox-pokrec-parametrami` — open exploration of σ / k / σ_s / σ_r.
**Sources**: 5 lesson-level (Tomasi & Manduchi 1998, scikit-image docs, Szeliski 2022, OpenCV tutorial, Wikipedia) plus section-level entries on the two theory beats.
**Assets generated** (all local, all on disk, no external URLs in image positions):
- `assets/images/cameraman-clean-vs-noisy.png`, `assets/images/gauss-median-bilateral-triple.png`
- `assets/plots/gauss-median-bilateral-na-optyce-1.png` (reproduces from `sourceCode` byte-for-byte)
- `assets/inputs/gauss-median-bilateral-cameraman-noisy.png`, `assets/inputs/gauss-median-bilateral-cameraman-expected.png`
